## Why This Is Asked

Tests diagnosing certificate rotation within a service mesh, focusing on end-to-end TLS verification, per-tenant isolation, and zero-downtime deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- TLS certificate rotation propagation across Kubernetes secrets and Envoy proxies
- mTLS handshake troubleshooting in Istio service mesh
- Canary rollouts with automated rollback capabilities
- Per-tenant routing and isolation in multi-tenant mesh environments

## Code Example

```javascript
// TLS handshake tester (pseudo)
async function testTLS(target) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(target);
    return response.ok;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor certificate expiration dates across all pods?
- What metrics would you use to detect TLS handshake failures in real-time?
- How do you ensure tenant isolation during certificate rotation?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cache coherence and multi-tenant latency debugging at scale with Istio and Redis. Requires concrete commands and safe rollout strategy.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant caching, TTL-based refresh, cache stampede
- Istio telemetry, per-tenant quotas, Redis keyspace
- Canary rollouts, rollback safety, latency targets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: TTL check for a tenant cache key
async function ttlForTenant(tenantId) {
  const key = `tenant:${tenantId}`;
  const ttl = await redis.ttl(key);
  return ttl;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect cache stampede and mitigate with mutexes or probabilistic TTLs?
- How would you verify rollout safety without affecting other tenants?

Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical debugging of startup-time issues caused by a sidecar container, including readiness ordering and configuration mounting verification, plus safe rollback procedures while maintaining latency targets. It emphasizes concrete kubectl usage and observable outcomes in a real-world production scenario.

Key Concepts
- Kubernetes rollout status and readiness probe verification
- Sidecar container impact on startup sequencing and latency
- ConfigMap and Secret mounting validation techniques
- Zero-downtime rollback strategies with latency constraints
- Production debugging workflow under load conditions

Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Node.js snippet for monitoring deployment status
const k8s = require('@kubernetes/client-node');
const kc = new k8s.KubeConfig();
kc.loadFromDefault();

const appsV1 = kc.makeApiClient(k8s.AppsV1Api);
const watch = new k8s.Watch(kc);

async function monitorRollout(namespace, deployment) {
  const stream = await watch.watch(`/apis/apps/v1/namespaces/${namespace}/deployments/${deployment}`,
    {}, // watch options
    (type, obj) => {
      if (obj.status.readyReplicas === obj.spec.replicas) {
        console.log('Rollout completed successfully');
      }
    });
}
```
